Thanks @wkania, the premise is right and verified, the docs have promised this since the `date_point` type shipped. I rebased on 8.2, squashed with your authorship and hardened the pass on three axes:

* `setTypedFieldMapper()` replaces, so appending our call silently discarded a mapper the application configured through DoctrineBundle's `typed_field_mapper` option. An existing call is now wrapped in `ChainTypedFieldMapper` with the application's mapper first;
* only `doctrine.orm.default_configuration` was covered; the pass now iterates every `doctrine.orm.*_configuration`, so multi-entity-manager setups get the mapping everywhere;
* `DayPoint` and `TimePoint` had the identical docs gap, and the same pass already registers their DBAL types, so the map covers all three.

Plus a `class_exists(DefaultTypedFieldMapper::class)` guard for ORM versions without typed field mapping. Each behaviour has a test, the bridge suite is green at 481, and restoring the original pass fails 3 of the new tests.
